# LabPilot — environment variables template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own keys:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` holds real secrets and is git-ignored — never commit it.
# This file (`.env.example`) holds no secrets and IS committed,
# so anyone cloning the repo knows which keys the project needs.
#
# Rewritten 2026-08-11: Cerebras died (card now required), Modal left the
# generator chain, Mistral joined, and the chain was re-ordered on measured
# benchmarks. See CLAUDE.md -> "The three chains".
#
# Updated 2026-08-17: tier numbers removed everywhere (they went stale twice in
# one day — route by model name), Google's quota corrected from a fictional
# "~1,500/day" to the measured per-model numbers, GLM-5.2 marked dead, and Groq
# given a real section instead of a trailing note.


# --- Google AI Studio (Gemini) ----------------------------------------------
# GENERATOR  gemini-3.7-flash, 3.6-flash, 3.5-flash   <- the top of the chain
# GENERATOR  gemini-3.5-flash-lite, 3.1-flash-lite    <- the volume workhorses
# GENERATOR  gemma-4-31b                              <- blocked until Step 1
# EMBEDDER   backup  gemini-embedding-001
#
# Get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/api-keys
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-16, replacing a "~1,500 requests/day" figure that was simply
# wrong. The quota is PER MODEL, not per key:
#     Flash       20/day each   <- yes, twenty
#     Flash-Lite  500/day each
#     Gemma       14,400/day each
# So Google's BEST models give 60 requests a day between them, and its cheap
# ones give 1,000. That asymmetry is the whole argument for model routing.
#
# Chat and embedding are SEPARATE quotas, so using Google for both is fine.
#
# Model names are listed here instead of tier numbers on purpose: tier indices
# went stale twice in one day. Route by model name.
#
# Note: on the free tier, prompts may be used to improve Google's products.
# Note: do NOT use this account behind a VPN or location switcher — that is what
#       got the first Google account permanently restricted (403).
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# A SECOND Google account. Not a spare key - a second QUOTA: Google bills
# per project per model, so every Gemini and Gemma model gets a fresh daily
# allowance on this one. The chain carries each Google model twice, with the
# key in its quota_pool, so one spent account never retires the other.
GOOGLE_API_KEY_2=


# --- Mistral -----------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATOR  mistral-medium, magistral-small  <- both are reasoning models
# GENERATOR  devstral-2512                    <- code-writing specialist
# GENERATOR  glm-5-2                          <- DEAD: allocation is now zero,
#                                                kept so a revival shows as XPASS
# EMBEDDER   PRIMARY codestral-embed          <- code-specific, 1536 dimensions
#
# Get a key: https://console.mistral.ai
# Phone verification required. No credit card.
#
# Limits are per-model RATE limits (tokens/min, requests/sec) plus a monthly
# consumption cap — so it throttles rather than dying, but it is not unlimited.
# Check the account's own Limits and Subscription pages for the monthly number.
#
# Mistral has NO reranker — verified 2026-08-11, zero matches in GET /v1/models.
MISTRAL_API_KEY=


# --- OpenRouter --------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATOR  nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free
# GENERATOR  nvidia/nemotron-3-super:free
# GENERATOR  cohere/north-mini-code:free
#
# Get a key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
#
# REQUIRED SETTING: in OpenRouter Settings, enable
#   "Allow free endpoints that train on request data"
# Without it, every `:free` model returns an error.
#
# ~50 requests/day AND 20 requests/minute, global per account. Both tiers share
# that one pool. This is the scarcest quota in the project, so spend it ONLY on
# generation — never on embedding or reranking.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=


# --- Cohere ------------------------------------------------------------------
# RERANKER primary  rerank-v4.0-fast / rerank-v4.0-pro
#
# Get a key: https://dashboard.cohere.com
# VERIFIED LIVE 2026-08-11 — trial key, no credit card required.
#
# Trial keys are free but capped at 1,000 API CALLS PER MONTH across chat,
# embed AND rerank combined. Too small to split, so Cohere gets exactly one
# job: reranking. Rerank auto-chunks documents over 510 tokens, which silently
# multiplies the billed count — keep chunks under that.
#
# Rerank has no playground UI; it is API-only at POST /v2/rerank.
#
# Cohere is ALSO the last-resort embedder (embed-v4.0, 128K input context) --
# deliberately last, because a corpus migrated here stays locked to Cohere and
# every future query would then spend the same bucket the reranker needs.
COHERE_API_KEY=


# --- Voyage AI ----------------------------------------------------------------
# RERANKER secondary  rerank-2.5-lite
#
# Get a key: https://dash.voyageai.com
# VERIFIED LIVE 2026-08-11 — no credit card required.
#
# 200 MILLION free rerank tokens, ONE-TIME per account (not monthly). At ~25K
# tokens per call that is roughly 8,000 reranks. Rate limits are generous:
# 4M tokens/min, 2,000 requests/min.
#
# Ordered BELOW Cohere on purpose: Cohere's 1,000/month renews whether it is
# used or not, so spend that first and bank the one-time grant.
VOYAGE_API_KEY=


# --- Cloudflare Workers AI ----------------------------------------------------
# RERANKER  @cf/baai/bge-reranker-base
# EMBEDDER  option  @cf/baai/bge-small|base|large-en-v1.5  (also runs locally)
# GENERATOR  @cf/openai/gpt-oss-120b  <- outage insurance only
#
# Get a token: https://dash.cloudflare.com
# VERIFIED LIVE 2026-08-11 — no credit card required.
# The token needs BOTH `Workers AI - Read` and `Workers AI - Edit`.
#
# Billed in "Neurons": 10,000/day free, shared across generation, embedding and
# reranking. At LabPilot's prompt size that is only ~11 generation calls/day, so
# keep Cloudflare for the cheap jobs (rerank/embed) rather than generation.
CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=


# --- Modal --------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT part of the generator chain any more (removed 2026-08-11).
# Its only job is Step 4: serving the fine-tuned model (Gemma 4 + our LoRA
# adapter) from the $30 Starter credit.
#
# Get a key: https://modal.com
# Leave blank until Step 4. Nothing in Step 0 reads it.
MODAL_API_KEY=


# --- Cerebras (DEAD — kept as a warning) --------------------------------------
# Verified 2026-08-11: the API now returns
#   HTTP 402 {"code":"payment_required"}
# and the dashboard demands a payment method before any request runs. The key
# showed as ACTIVE, but that is the KEY's state, not the ACCOUNT's API access.
#
# Lesson: an issued API key is not a working API. A platform counts as verified
# only once a request has returned a token.
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# --- Cline --------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATOR  z-ai/glm-5.3-flash  (tier 1)
#
# Get a key: https://app.cline.bot -> Settings -> API Keys
# VERIFIED LIVE 2026-09-13 - no credit card required.
#
# FREE, and free in a way no other entry here is: Cline records what the call
# WOULD have cost and charges ZERO credits for it. Measured - two 1,700-token
# generations reported costUsd 84,625 and 78,375 with creditsUsed 0, while a
# paid control model deducted credit immediately on 13 tokens.
#
# THE QUOTA IS PUBLISHED NOWHERE. Not in the docs, not on any endpoint, and
# Cline sends NO rate-limit headers at all - so unlike every other provider
# here we cannot tell "busy" from "spent", and the first 429 will retire the
# pool. Watch the `cost` field in the log: the free promotion ending shows up
# there first, as a credit deduction.
#
# Only 2 of Cline's 6 free models answer the API. The other four return
# 403 "only available via Cline product surfaces" - the reachable pair is
# z-ai/glm-5.3-flash and poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free.
CLINE_API_KEY=


# --- Groq ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATOR  gpt-oss-120b
#
# Get a key: https://console.groq.com
# VERIFIED LIVE 2026-08-17 — no credit card required.
#
# 1,000 requests/day, one of the largest budgets here, against only 8,000
# tokens/MINUTE counting prompt AND reserved output together. So a full report
# is impossible and always will be, but Step 2's small jobs fit easily.
# _check_fits refuses it locally, so it costs no request while unreachable.
# Groq offers no embedding models at all.
# Kilo resells OpenRouter under its OWN org account, so these tiers are a
# SECOND free allowance for models we already reach: 200 requests per HOUR
# against OpenRouter's 50 per DAY. Measured - three Kilo calls left our
# OpenRouter counter untouched at 17 of 50.
#
# The key is OPTIONAL. Kilo's docs say anonymous and authenticated free
# requests are rate-limited identically, BY IP - so on a shared VPN exit the
# 200/hour is split with everyone else on that address. It sends no
# rate-limit headers and has no usage endpoint, so the remaining allowance
# cannot be read.
# app.kilo.ai -> Your Profile -> Integrations -> API Key (already generated)
# Requesty - a THIRD free route, independent of both Google and OpenRouter.
# 200 requests a DAY, no card, no trial expiry. Its value is independence,
# not new capability: a refused Google exit has already cost this project
# every Google tier for a week, and Requesty serves Gemma and Nemotron
# without touching Google or OpenRouter.
# Measured 2026-09-19: 7 of its 12 free models answer. No usage or credits
# endpoint exists, so the remaining allowance cannot be read.
# app.requesty.ai/sign-up -> app.requesty.ai/api-keys
REQUESTY_API_KEY=

KILO_API_KEY=

GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- gateways MEASURED 2026-09-23, none of them wired into CHAIN yet -----------
# Five platforms were probed live on the same afternoon. Every number below is
# a real call, not a pricing page. See CLAUDE.md section 10.5.
#
# LiteRouter - the strongest find. 454 models, 42 free, and THREE of them are
# dead or unreachable everywhere else we have: deepseek-v4-flash-0731:free (the
# exact model OpenRouter retired that same day), glm-5.3-flash:free (our TIER 1
# MODEL, otherwise only on Cline whose quota is published nowhere) and
# glm-5.2:free (dead on Mistral, congested on OpenRouter).
#   measured  7 of 10 models tested answer. Function calling 3 of 3.
#             48,011 real prompt tokens accepted - a full report FITS.
#   quota     NOT PUBLISHED. No rate-limit headers; /v1/key /v1/usage /v1/me
#             /v1/credits /v1/limits /v1/quota all 404. Third tier in this
#             project flying blind, after Cline and Token Harbor.
#   TRAP      ONE CONCURRENT REQUEST. It answers 403 "Too many concurrent
#             requests" even to SEQUENTIAL calls, when an earlier request has
#             timed out on our side but is still running on theirs. We model
#             requests/day and tokens/minute and NOT concurrency, so slice 3's
#             parallel nodes can break this while inside every quota we track.
# docs.literouter.com -> sign up -> API key.  Base https://api.literouter.com/v1
LITEROUTER_API_KEY=

# OrcaRouter - the only one that PUBLISHES its free limits in a machine-readable
# place: GET /api/free-package/public.
#   quota     10 requests/minute, 50/day for an account that has never paid.
#             20 rpm / 800 rpd after $20 of lifetime spend.
#   measured  4 of 4 free models answer, 2.4-4.5s. 15,691 real prompt tokens
#             accepted, so a full report fits.
#   free      deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-free · z-ai/glm-5.3-flash-free ·
#             tencent/hy3-free · orca/orcaverify-text1.0-free (own override,
#             5 rpm / 50 rpd) · orcarouter/free (auto-routes the free lineup)
#   NOTE      glm-5.3-flash returns EMPTY CONTENT without reasoning.effort and
#             'ok' with it - exactly as recorded for Cline. So that is a
#             property of the MODEL, and every route to GLM-5.3 needs it.
# orcarouter.ai -> console.  Base https://api.orcarouter.ai/v1
ORCAROUTER_API_KEY=

# Routeway - states its quota in the RESPONSE HEADERS, which nobody else does:
#   x-ratelimit-limit-minute: 5 · x-ratelimit-limit-day: 200
#   measured  deepseek-v4-flash:free 3 of 3 on retry. Its first two attempts
#             answered 429 "temporarily overloaded" - THEIR congestion, not our
#             quota, which still read remaining-day 199.
#   free      deepseek-v4-flash:free · minimax-m2.7:free · muse-glimmer-30b:free
# routeway.ai.  Base https://api.routeway.ai/v1
ROUTEWAY_API_KEY=

# Token Harbor - works, and its failure mode is a HANG rather than an error.
#   measured  8 of 20 rounds. Successes are FAST and uniform, 0.7-1.6s.
#             Failures never return at all.
#   SHAPE     the failures are TIME-CORRELATED, not independent: rounds 1-13
#             gave 1 success in 78 calls, rounds 14-20 gave 7 in 11. So MORE
#             RETRIES IS THE WRONG LEVER - during a bad window six retries fail
#             as surely as one.
#   policy    1 try, ~3s cap, then mark the tier dead for a few minutes. That is
#             the dead_pools shape we already have in llm/chain.py. A 2s cap was
#             rejected: real answers were measured at 2.86-4.44s.
#   WARNING   our global DEFAULT_TIMEOUT read is 600s. ONE hung call here would
#             spend 600 of the 900s budget. Timeout must become per provider.
#   free      deepseek-v4-flash:free · deepseek-v4.1-flash:free ·
#             qwen3.8-flash:free (CLAUDE.md says Qwen3.8-Flash has no free
#             no-card route anywhere - this OVERTURNS that) ·
#             mimo-v2.5:free · mimo-v2.6-flash:free
#   NOTE      its final SSE chunk carries an EMPTY choices list; a parser that
#             assumes choices[0] crashes on it.
# tokenharbor.ai - the API is blocked until the signup email is VERIFIED, and
# the refusal is a clean typed 403 that says so.  Base https://tokenharbor.ai/v1
TOKEN_HARBOR_API=

# TeamoRouter - advertises a permanent free tier, 50/day, no card. All three of
# its free models answer 400 "Your TeamoRouter wallet balance is insufficient".
# Recorded so nobody re-tests it on the strength of the marketing page; it may
# need the free tier claimed on the dashboard first.
# api.teamorouter.com/v1 (also .cn)
TEAMROUTER_API_KEY=

# Zen / OpenCode - UNUSABLE, and it says so in a typed error: every free model
# answers FreeTierError "OpenCode's free tier can only be used from within
# OpenCode". Identical with Bearer, with x-api-key, and with NO KEY AT ALL, so
# it is a CLIENT GATE, not auth. Getting past it would mean presenting our code
# as the OpenCode CLI, which we do not do. The key is not needed.
ZEN_API_KEY=


# --- API tuning (optional) -----------------------------------------------------
# Every one of these has a working default in `labpilot/api/config.py`. They are
# listed here because ApiConfig reads them from the environment, and a knob
# nobody knows about is a knob nobody can turn.
#
# MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES — per-file ceiling for each side of a comparison. Default
# 1000000, the same 1MB the repo walk uses. Note the real working limit is
# usually lower: an artifact is refused with 413 when its outline alone exceeds
# the prompt budget, which happens around 700-800 parts. Step 1 raises that by
# listing files instead of chunks.
MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=

# MAX_REQUEST_BODY_BYTES — whole multipart body ceiling, checked by middleware
# BEFORE parsing. Defaults to 2 x MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES + 65536 for boundaries and
# headers. This is the memory guard; MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES is what users are told.
MAX_REQUEST_BODY_BYTES=

# CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS — comma separated. Empty (the default) adds no CORS
# middleware at all, which is correct for an API with no browser client yet.
CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS=

# FRONTEND_DIR — the static page mounted at /ui. Defaults to `web/` beside the
# package. It is mounted only when the directory exists, so an API-only
# deployment can simply not ship it.
FRONTEND_DIR=


# --- Supabase Postgres + pgvector ----------------------------------------------
# STORE  the chunks table and its vectors (slice 4).
#
# Get it: Supabase dashboard -> Connect -> Session pooler.
#
# USE THE SESSION POOLER, NOT THE DIRECT CONNECTION. Measured 2026-09-03:
# `db.<project-ref>.supabase.co` did not resolve on IPv4 or IPv6 from here,
# because direct connections are IPv6-only unless you buy the IPv4 add-on.
# The pooler answers over IPv4 and needs no add-on.
#
# USE PORT 5432, NEVER 6543. Same host serves both: 5432 is SESSION mode,
# 6543 is TRANSACTION mode, and transaction mode rejects prepared statements --
# which psycopg3 uses by default. The failure reads
# `prepared statement "_pg3_0" already exists`, so it looks like a bug in our
# code and is not.
#
# THE USER IS NOT `postgres`. The pooler serves many projects, so the username
# carries the project ref and tells it which database is yours.
#
# Verified live 2026-09-03: PostgreSQL 17.6, pgvector 0.8.2 already installed --
# so the schema needs no CREATE EXTENSION, and hnsw.iterative_scan (new in
# 0.8.0) is available for filtered vector search.
#
# postgresql://postgres.PROJECT-REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
DATABASE_URL=
